---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Pricing & insurance · Direct Lifestyle Medicine" active="pricing" bookbar={true}>

  <!-- 1 · Intro -->
  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Pricing</h1>
      <p class="lede">What $99 covers, what it doesn&rsquo;t, and what to
      do if $99 is out of reach.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2 · The price card + the three memberships -->
  <section class="section band-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split even" style="align-items:start">
        <div class="price-card">
          <div class="amt">$99 <span>per month</span></div>
          <div class="per">per adult patient &middot; no per-visit charges</div>
          <ul class="check-list">
            <li>An ongoing relationship with one doctor</li>
            <li>A full first assessment of your health, history,
            medicines, and habits</li>
            <li>An individual written plan, reviewed as you go</li>
            <li>Visits as your care needs them: by video, at home when
            needed, or in a clinic</li>
            <li>Direct messaging, answered in 1&ndash;2 business days</li>
            <li>Every result reviewed and explained</li>
            <li>Medical care and treatment within my scope, including
            prescriptions I write</li>
            <li>Referrals and coordination with your other doctors</li>
            <li>Forms and paperwork included: disability, FMLA, letters,
            prior authorizations</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small" style="margin-bottom:20px;color:var(--soft)">
            No enrollment fee. No contract. Cancel anytime, effective at
            the end of your billing month. Pay monthly by card or bank
            account.
          </p>
          <a class="btn" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
          <p class="small" style="margin-top:16px"><a class="quiet" style="font-size:14.5px" href="/agreement">Read the membership agreement &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2>Three fee levels, the same care</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Every member gets the same assessment, plan, access to me,
            and treatment within my scope, whatever they pay.
          </p>
          <div class="rows" style="margin-top:clamp(24px,3vw,34px)">
            <div class="row">
              <b>Standard</b>
              <p>$99 a month per adult. Each adult enrolls individually,
              so a couple is $198. I care for adults only.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
              <b>Sliding scale</b>
              <p>A reduced monthly fee based on your finances. There is
              no application form. We talk about it, and I use simple
              written criteria so it stays fair.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
              <b>Pro bono</b>
              <p>A small number of free memberships, for people who could
              not otherwise afford this care. How many I can offer depends
              on how full the practice is.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="small soft" style="margin-top:22px">
            If cost is the problem, say so when we talk. You do not need
            to prove anything to ask.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3 · What the fee does not cover -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>What the fee does not cover</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            My fee covers my work as your doctor. Care from others is
            billed by them, usually through your insurance.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Labs</b>
          <p>Through your insurance. Where I can get discounted direct
          pricing, I pass it to you at my cost and tell you the number
          before anything is drawn.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Imaging</b>
          <p>Through your insurance. I order what is needed and explain
          the results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicines</b>
          <p>Your pharmacy and insurance, as now. I help you find fair
          prices. Texas law does not allow doctors to sell medicines.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Specialists</b>
          <p>Through your insurance. I refer you and stay involved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Urgent care, ER, hospital</b>
          <p>Through your insurance, as today. My fee never replaces
          coverage for these.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        <p class="prose" style="margin-top:28px">
          So I recommend every member keep health coverage. The
          membership works alongside insurance, not instead of it. It
          is also not a promise to manage every medical condition you
          have.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4 · How your coverage fits -->
  <section class="section band-warm" id="bookbar-after">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>How your coverage fits</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            I do not bill insurance, Medicare, or Medicaid. You pay me
            directly, and your coverage keeps working for everything
            else.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <div class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="row">
          <b>Private insurance, or none</b>
          <p>Sign up. That is all. Your plan is not involved in our
          agreement, and your insurance status does not change the price
          or the care.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>Medicare or Medicaid</b>
          <p>I want to be able to serve you. How a direct membership
          works with these programs is still being settled with my
          lawyer. Ask me in the free conversation and I will tell you
          where it stands.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <b>HSA and FSA funds</b>
          <p>Possibly. Whether these funds can pay a membership like this
          one depends on how the practice is finally structured. Confirm
          with your tax advisor, and ask me what I know at the time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5 · Why $99, and the limits -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <h2>Why $99, and what&rsquo;s the catch</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            I can charge $99 because the practice is small: no office
            building, no billing department, no staff, and a limited
            number of patients I know. The low price is also what makes
            the sliding scale and the free memberships possible.
          </p>
          <p>
            The limits: I keep business hours. I am not an emergency
            service. I treat within my scope and
            refer when something is outside it. I take real time away
            each year. And when my panel is full, it is full.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a class="quiet" href="/agreement">Read the full membership agreement &rarr;</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 6 · CTA -->
  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <h2>Questions about your situation?</h2>
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
